# Shaydor Intel

## Lore

The intel are the insect-headed cousins of the shaydor spherians: tall,
spindly stilt-people with huge bug eyes, antennae and a hard, bony skin,
though they are mammals. They are quicker and more aggressive than the
gentle spherians while sharing their curiosity and quiet manner. Where the
spherians are master psionics, the intel have only a few psionic powers but a
strong resistance to psionic attack and mind control - likely a result of the
long, rarely lethal rivalry between the two shaydor peoples, and the two still
dislike each other.

Many intel serve the Splugorth willingly and can rise high among the Minions,
and they fetch a good price at the slave market, especially as mechanics.
Others oppose the Splugorth fanatically and hate their kin who serve them; on
Earth some are rumored to have allied with the True Atlanteans. Still others
have left to settle new worlds or wander as adventurers. They use no magic of
their own, but will collect and use magic items and any kind of weapon.

## GM Notes

Optional player character and monster. NPCs average level 1D4+2; player
characters start at first level on the mind melter''s experience table.
